  Company Credits section body.

  Lists the company's credit records with the shared live search and the shared pagination control.

  A credit is specific to a course plus an access period, and it is not permanently consumed until
  the learner explicitly starts the course - before commencement it can be unassigned and returned.
  The four counts are shown separately for that reason: total, available, assigned and consumed are
  four different states, and collapsing them would hide the one an administrator needs.

  WARNING: a template comment is not a safe place to document syntax. A comment delimiter
  written inside a comment body ends the comment early and leaks the remainder onto the page.
  Keep every comment plain prose: no comment delimiters and no code, not even to document one.
